    "rendered": "<div class=\"xyz-content\">\n<nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\" class=\"shell pt-6\">\n<ol class=\"m-0 flex list-none flex-wrap items-center gap-2 p-0 text-[0.8125rem] text-ink-soft\">\n<li class=\"flex items-center gap-2\">  <a href=\"/\" class=\"no-underline hover:underline\"> Home </a> </li>\n<li class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"> <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-rule\"> / </span> <a href=\"/calculators/\" class=\"no-underline hover:underline\"> Calculators </a> </li>\n<li class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"> <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-rule\"> / </span> <span aria-current=\"page\">GST</span> </li>\n</ol>\n</nav>\n<div class=\"shell pt-6\">\n<p class=\"band-eyebrow\">Free calculator</p>\n<h1 class=\"max-w-3xl text-3xl sm:text-4xl\">GST calculator</h1>\n<p class=\"mt-3 max-w-2xl text-[1.0625rem]\">Add 10% GST to a price, or find the GST already inside one. The second is the one people get wrong.</p>\n<p class=\"m-0 font-mono text-[0.75rem] tabular-nums text-ink-soft mt-4\"> Updated for 2024–25, 2025–26, 2026–27 · verified against <a href=\"https://www.ato.gov.au/tax-rates-and-codes/tax-rates-australian-residents\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">ato.gov.au</a> on 2026-08-21 · some 2026–27 thresholds are provisional pending ATO indexation </p>\n</p></div>\n<div class=\"shell mt-8\">\n<div id=\"xyz-island-0\" data-xyz-island=\"GstCalculator\" data-xyz-props=\"{}\">\n<div class=\"grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_23rem] lg:gap-12\">\n<div class=\"min-w-0\">\n<div class=\"rounded-[4px] border border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-white px-4 sm:px-6\">\n<fieldset class=\"border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] py-4 last:border-b-0 m-0 p-0\">\n<legend class=\"mb-2 p-0 text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)]\">What do you want to do?</legend>\n<div class=\"flex flex-wrap gap-1 rounded-[4px] border border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-white p-1\"><button type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"true\" class=\"flex-1 whitespace-nowrap rounded-[2px] px-3 py-1.5 text-[0.8125rem] transition-colors bg-[var(--color-ink)] font-semibold text-[var(--color-paper)]\">Find the GST in a price</button><button type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\" class=\"flex-1 whitespace-nowrap rounded-[2px] px-3 py-1.5 text-[0.8125rem] transition-colors text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] hover:bg-[var(--color-paper-sunk)]\">Add GST to a price</button></div>\n</fieldset>\n<div class=\"py-4 border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] last:border-b-0\">\n<div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3\"><label for=\"_r1R_4l_\" class=\"text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)]\">Amount including GST</label></div>\n<div class=\"mt-2\">\n<div class=\"relative\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute left-3 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 font-mono text-sm text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">$</span><input id=\"_r1R_4l_\" type=\"text\" inputMode=\"decimal\" autoComplete=\"off\" class=\"w-full rounded-[4px] border border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-white px-3 py-2.5 text-[var(--color-ink)] focus:border-[var(--color-signal)] pl-7 text-right\" placeholder=\"0\" value=\"1,100\"/></div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"mt-1.5 mb-0 text-[0.75rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">The total on the invoice or receipt.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"mt-4\">\n<div class=\"rounded-[4px] border border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-white p-5\">\n<h2 class=\"m-0 font-display text-base font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]\">Why it is one eleventh, not ten per cent</h2>\n<p class=\"mt-2 mb-0 text-[0.8125rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">GST is 10% of the pre-GST price, so a <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$100</span> item becomes <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$110</span>. Working backwards from <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$110,</span> the GST is <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$10</span> — which is one eleventh of <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$110,</span> not 10% of it. Taking 10% off the inclusive figure gives <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$11,</span> and that error compounds across a whole BAS.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"min-w-0 lg:sticky lg:top-6 lg:self-start\">\n<div class=\"overflow-hidden rounded-[4px] border border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-white\">\n<div class=\"flex items-center justify-between gap-3 border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-[var(--color-ink)] px-4 py-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-[var(--color-paper)]\">GST</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.6875rem] tabular-nums text-[var(--color-paper)]/70\">10%</span></div>\n<div class=\"tally-print\">\n<div data-tally-line=\"exclusive\" class=\"border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] \">\n<div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-2.5\"><button type=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 text-left text-[0.8125rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] hover:text-[var(--color-ink)]\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"inline-block text-[0.625rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] transition-transform \">▶</span>Price excluding GST</button><span class=\"shrink-0 text-[0.9375rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"font-mono text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\"></span><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums \" aria-hidden=\"true\">$1,000</span></span></div>\n</div>\n<div data-tally-line=\"gst\" class=\"border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] \">\n<div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-2.5\"><button type=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 text-left text-[0.8125rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] hover:text-[var(--color-ink)]\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"inline-block text-[0.625rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] transition-transform \">▶</span>GST</button><span class=\"shrink-0 text-[0.9375rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"font-mono text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\"></span><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums \" aria-hidden=\"true\">$100</span></span></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div data-tally-line=\"inclusive\" class=\"px-4 py-5\">\n<div class=\"flex items-end justify-between gap-4\">\n<div>\n<p class=\"m-0 text-[0.8125rem] font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)]\">Price including GST</p>\n<p class=\"m-0 mt-0.5 max-w-[22rem] text-[0.6875rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">What the customer pays.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"flex h-11 shrink-0 items-center\"><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums text-[1.75rem] font-bold text-[var(--color-ink)]\" aria-hidden=\"true\">$1,100</span></div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"sr-only\" aria-live=\"polite\">Price including GST<!-- -->:<!-- --> <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$1,100</span></p>\n<div class=\"mt-4\">\n<p class=\"m-0 text-[0.6875rem] leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">GST-free and input-taxed supplies exist — food, most health and education, residential rent. If you sell any of those, not everything you invoice carries GST.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div data-testid=\"sticky-result\" class=\"fixed inset-x-0 bottom-0 z-40 border-t border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-white/95 backdrop-blur lg:hidden\">\n<div class=\"mx-auto flex max-w-[68rem] items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3\">\n<div class=\"min-w-0\">\n<p class=\"m-0 truncate text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">GST included</p>\n<p class=\"m-0 font-mono text-lg font-bold tabular-nums text-[var(--color-ink)]\">$100</p>\n</div>\n<p><a href=\"/lodge/\" class=\"shrink-0 rounded-[4px] bg-[var(--color-ink)] px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-paper)] no-underline\">Lodge</a></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"h-20 lg:hidden\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n<p><!--astro:end--></div>\n</p></div>\n<div class=\"shell mt-8\">\n<p class=\"m-0 max-w-2xl text-[0.8125rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft\"> This is an estimate, not tax advice. It works from the figures you enter and the ATO rates for the year you selected; your actual assessment is determined by the ATO and may differ. We never ask for your tax file number on this site. </p>\n</p></div>\n<div class=\"shell mt-16\">\n<div class=\"prose-statement\">\n<h2>Getting the BAS figures right</h2>\n<p> Your BAS wants GST-exclusive amounts at G1 and the GST itself at 1A and 1B. Most accounting software handles the split, but manual entries and cash-basis reconciliations are where the one eleventh rule earns its keep. </p>\n<p> A worked example. You invoice <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-ink text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$5,500</span> including GST. The GST is  <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-ink text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$500</span> — one eleventh — and your income is  <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-ink text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$5,000</span>. Take 10% off the <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-ink text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$5,500</span> instead and you would report <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-ink text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$550</span> of GST and <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-ink text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$4,950</span> of income, overstating the GST payable and understating your income at the same time. </p>\n<h2>The GST you collect is not your money</h2>\n<p> From the moment a customer pays you, one eleventh of that payment belongs to the ATO. The businesses that get into trouble with GST are almost never the ones that miscalculated it — they are the ones that spent it. Move it out the day it arrives. </p>\n<h2>Tax invoices</h2>\n<p> For a purchase over <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-ink text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$82.50</span> including GST you need a valid tax invoice to claim the credit: the supplier&#8217;s identity and ABN, the date, a description, the GST amount and the words &#8220;tax invoice&#8221;. A bank statement line is not enough, and this is the first thing checked in a GST review. </p>\n</p></div>\n</p></div>\n<section class=\"shell mt-20\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-gst-calculator-heading\">\n<h2 id=\"faq-gst-calculator-heading\" class=\"text-2xl\">Questions people actually ask</h2>\n<dl class=\"mt-6 border-t border-rule\">\n<div class=\"border-b border-rule py-5\">\n<dt class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink\">How do I work out the GST in a price?</dt>\n<dd class=\"m-0 mt-2 max-w-3xl text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft\">Divide the GST-inclusive price by 11. On a <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$110</span> invoice the GST is <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$10</span>. Taking 10% off the inclusive price gives <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$11,</span> which is wrong — a mistake worth about 9% of your GST claims across a year.</dd>\n</p></div>\n<div class=\"border-b border-rule py-5\">\n<dt class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink\">When do I have to register for GST?</dt>\n<dd class=\"m-0 mt-2 max-w-3xl text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft\">When your turnover reaches <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$75,000</span> in any 12-month period, or when you expect it will. Non-profits have a <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$150,000</span> threshold. Taxi and ride-share drivers must register regardless of turnover.</dd>\n</p></div>\n<div class=\"border-b border-rule py-5\">\n<dt class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink\">What is not subject to GST?</dt>\n<dd class=\"m-0 mt-2 max-w-3xl text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft\">Basic food, most health and medical services, most education, childcare, and exports are GST-free. Residential rent and most financial supplies are input-taxed, which means no GST is charged and no credits can be claimed on related costs.</dd>\n</p></div>\n<div class=\"border-b border-rule py-5\">\n<dt class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink\">Can I claim GST on business purchases?</dt>\n<dd class=\"m-0 mt-2 max-w-3xl text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-soft\">Yes, if you are registered — you claim the GST credit on purchases used in your business, provided you hold a valid tax invoice for anything over <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$82.50</span>. You cannot claim credits on purchases relating to input-taxed supplies.</dd>\n</p></div>\n</dl>\n</section>\n<section class=\"shell mt-20\">\n<h2 class=\"text-xl\">Read up first</h2>\n<ul class=\"mt-5 grid list-none gap-4 p-0 sm:grid-cols-2\">\n<li class=\"card p-5\">\n<h3 class=\"text-base\"><a href=\"/tax-tips/tax-deductions-for-sole-traders/\" class=\"text-ink no-underline hover:underline\">Tax deductions for sole traders and contractors</a></h3>\n<p class=\"mt-2 mb-0 text-[0.8125rem] text-ink-soft\">A sole trader claims business expenses rather than work-related ones, which widens what is available but also means the ATO expects records that stand up.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"cta-dark\">\n<div class=\"cta-grid\">\n<div>\n<p class=\"band-eyebrow\">Ready to lodge it?</p>\n<h2>A registered agent prepares it, checks it, and lodges it.</h2>\n<p>Most refunds land within two weeks of assessment. The fee is fixed and quoted before we start — nothing is charged until you approve the finished return.</p>\n<div class=\"cta-actions\"> <a href=\"/lodge/\" class=\"btn\">Start your return</a> <a href=\"/pricing/\" class=\"btn btn-secondary\">See pricing</a> </div>\n</p></div>\n<div class=\"cta-spec\">\n<div class=\"cta-spec-row\"><span>Individual returns from</span><b>$99</b></div>\n<div class=\"cta-spec-row\"><span>Registered tax agent</span><b>26233684</b></div>\n<div class=\"cta-spec-row\"><span>Fixed fee, quoted up front</span><i>included</i></div>\n<div class=\"cta-spec-row\"><span>Fee deductible from refund</span><i>included</i></div>\n</p></div>\n</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"shell mt-20\">\n<div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4\">\n<h2 class=\"text-xl\">Other calculators</h2>\n<p> <a href=\"/calculators/\" class=\"text-sm whitespace-nowrap\">All calculators →</a> </div>\n<ul class=\"mt-5 grid list-none gap-4 p-0 sm:grid-cols-3\">\n<li class=\"card p-5\"> <a href=\"/tax-calculator/\" class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink no-underline hover:underline\"> Income tax </a>\n<p class=\"mt-2 mb-0 text-[0.8125rem] text-ink-soft\">Your tax, Medicare levy, study loan repayment and take-home pay for any income, in any of the last three financial years.</p>\n</li>\n<li class=\"card p-5\"> <a href=\"/tax-refund-calculator/\" class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink no-underline hover:underline\"> Tax refund </a>\n<p class=\"mt-2 mb-0 text-[0.8125rem] text-ink-soft\">Estimate your refund by adding the deductions you actually have. Watch the number move as you claim.</p>\n</li>\n<li class=\"card p-5\"> <a href=\"/calculators/capital-gains-tax-calculator/\" class=\"font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink no-underline hover:underline\"> Capital gains </a>\n<p class=\"mt-2 mb-0 text-[0.8125rem] text-ink-soft\">What you will pay on a share, property or crypto sale — with the 50% discount and any carried-forward losses applied in the right order.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</div>\n<p><script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/brseeger-cloud/xyz-accounting-assets@main/islands/GstCalculator.js\" defer></script></p>\n"
  },
